> As a valk I should be picking up every spellbook for identification
> later? For some reason I was just assuming Valks couldn't do spells as
> they barely get any power whatsoever. What spells would have been
> largely useful for me?

Check the #enhance list and you'll see that you can advance
skills in two classes.  You should at least keep books in those
two schools and any you consider valuable anyways.  Early on
to me that means keeping them in a stash until I can BUC check
them, read all blessed ones.  Maybe even carry the cursed ones
during altar camping to move them to uncursed.

The special spell for a valk is cone of cold.  This matters a lot
on levels like Medusa where you can just blast a path to where
you want to go.  Run out of power?  Go explore a bit and come
back later.

Some of the best armor doesn't interfere with spell casting, so
a valk who pays a little attention to that can easily get well
past being able to cast cone of cold at 0% failure rate.  A very
overprepared Valk might get to near 60% failure rate for
identify.  That's a spell that can be retried at liesure away
from combat so retrying is not a problem.

Books aren't a priority but they are worth stashing and read
the blessed ones.

